\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\qc\ul\b\f0\fs32\lang9 Appium \par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\ulnone\b0\fs24 Appium is an open-source automation framework designed to test mobile applications. It supports native, hybrid, and mobile web applications on both iOS and Android platforms. It allows developers and testers to write tests using a wide variety of programming languages (e.g., Java, Python, JavaScript, Ruby, etc.) and execute them against mobile devices or emulators.\par

\pard\sl276\slmult1\ul\b Why Appium?\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl276\slmult1\ulnone Cross-Platform Support:\b0\par

\pard\sl276\slmult1 Appium enables a single API for both iOS and Android, meaning you can write tests that run on multiple platforms with little to no code modification.\par
\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl276\slmult1\b Supports Multiple Types of Apps:\b0\par

\pard\sl276\slmult1 Native Apps: Built with SDKs specific to Android or iOS.\par
Hybrid Apps: Contain a WebView for web-based content.\par
Mobile Web Apps: Accessed via mobile browsers like Safari or Chrome.\par
\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl276\slmult1\b Language Flexibility:\b0\par

\pard\sl276\slmult1 You can write tests in any language supported by Selenium WebDriver, making it developer-friendly.\par
\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl276\slmult1\b Open Source:\par

\pard\sl276\slmult1\b0 Free to use, with a large and active community providing support and updates.\par
\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl276\slmult1\b No Need to Modify Apps:\par

\pard\sl276\slmult1\b0 Unlike some tools, Appium doesn't require adding specific libraries or recompiling apps, preserving the app's original structure.\par
\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl276\slmult1\b Uses WebDriver Protocol:\par

\pard\sl276\slmult1\b0 Appium extends the Selenium WebDriver protocol to work with mobile-specific commands, providing a familiar experience for testers accustomed to Selenium.\par
\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl276\slmult1\b Real Device and Emulator/Simulator Support:\ul\par

\pard\sl276\slmult1\ulnone\b0 Tests can be run on physical devices, emulators, or simulators, ensuring flexibility.\par
\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl276\slmult1\b Extensible and Customizable:\b0\par

\pard\sl276\slmult1 Plugins and extensions can add functionality to Appium as per project requirements.\par
\par
\b\fs28 When to Use Appium:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl276\slmult1\b0\fs24 When you need cross-platform testing.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}When you want to automate functional tests for mobile applications.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}When your team prefers using WebDriver-based tools.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}When you require testing on real devices for accurate results.\par

\pard\sl276\slmult1\par
\par
\b In order to achieve this, Appium is effectively split into four parts:\par
\b0\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl276\slmult1  Appium Core - defines the core APIs\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab} Drivers - implement connectivity to specific platforms\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab} Clients - implement Appium's API in specific languages\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab} Plugins - change or extend Appium's core functionality\par

\pard\sl276\slmult1\par
\b\fs28 Basic setup on Windows \b0\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl276\slmult1\fs24 Check if node.js is installed and setup  --> node -v / npm -v\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b0\fs24 if its not download node.js in official website : {{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://nodejs.org/en/download/prebuilt-installer }}{\fldrslt{https://nodejs.org/en/download/prebuilt-installer\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs24  \b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b0\fs24 after download install node.js . it add path inside environment variable\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b0\fs24 Install Appium using CMD: \cf2 npm install -g appium@latest \cf0 / \cf2 npm i -g appium \cf0  \b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b0\fs24 Uninstall Appium using CMD : \cf2 npm uninstall -g appium \cf0 / \cf2 npm un -g appium \cf0\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b0\fs24 we you install appium2 its install only Appium server not the driver, we install driver separately\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b0\fs24 Checking Appium location : \cf2 where appium /which appium \cf0 and version using : \cf2 appium -v \cf0\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b0\fs24 Run Appium in CMD : \cf2 appium \cf0 it start server / \cf2 appium --allow-cors\cf0\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b0\fs24 Stop Appium sever press : CTRL + C\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b0\fs24 Install appium-doctor : is a handy tool from appium tream it fix common node.ios and android configuration issues.: \cf2 npm intall -g appium-doctor \cf0 / \cf2 npm install @appium/doctor --location=global\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\cf0\b0\fs24 for checking help : \cf2 appium-doctor --help \cf0 and cheking android : \cf2 appium-doctor --android\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\cf0\b0\fs24 To check Driver list : \cf2 appium driver list\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\cf0\b0\fs24 Install Driver : \cf2\b\fs28\par

\pard\sl276\slmult1\cf0\b0\fs24                       Android --> \cf2 appium driver insatll uiautomator2 \par
                      \cf0 IOS     --->  \cf2 appium driver insatll xcuitest\par

