\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\ul What is ANDROID SDK \ulnone : \fs24 The Android SDK (Software Development Kit) is a collection of tools, libraries, and APIs that developers use to build, test, and debug Android applications. It provides the necessary components to develop apps for Android devices, such as smartphones, tablets, smart TVs, and wearables.Includes tools like adb (Android Debug Bridge), fastboot, and the emulator.\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1  \ul\fs28 Platform Tools\ulnone\fs24 : Tools specific to the Android version you\rquote re targeting.Includes support for interacting with the Android platform, such as debugging and installing apps.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\ul\fs28 Build Tools\ulnone\fs24 : Compilers and tools used to build the APK (Android application package) from source code.Includes aapt, dx, and zipalign.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\ul\fs28 Android Emulator\ulnone\fs24 : A virtual device that simulates an Android environment for testing applications.\fs28\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\ul Cmdline-Tools:  \ulnone\fs24 These command-line utilities are useful for managing SDK packages and other tasks\fs28\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\par
