What are Android Command Line Tools?\par
\b0  collection of utilities provided by Google for Android app development and testing\par
These tools are essential for various tasks related to building, testing, managing devices, and debugging Android applications.\par
\par
\par
\b some key command-line tools:\par
\b0\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\b apkanalyzer\b0 :Provides insight into the composition of your APK (Android Package) after the build process completes. Helps you analyze the contents of your APK, including resources, classes, and dependencies.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b avdmanager\b0 :Allows you to create and manage Android Virtual Devices (AVDs) from the command line.Useful for setting up and configuring virtual devices for testing.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b lint\b0 : Scans your code to identify and correct problems related to the structural quality of your code. Helps maintain code consistency and adherence to best practices.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b retrace\b0 :Specifically useful for applications compiled by R8 (a code shrinker and obfuscator).Decodes obfuscated stack traces, mapping them back to your original source code.Helps debug issues in production by providing meaningful stack trace information.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b sdkmanager\b0 :Lets you view, install, update, and uninstall packages for the Android SDK.Use it to manage SDK components, including platform versions, build tools, and system images.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b AAPT2 (Android Asset Packaging Tool):\b0 Parses, indexes, and compiles Android resources (such as layouts, drawables, and strings) into a binary format optimized for the Android platform.Packages the compiled resources into a single output (APK).\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b apksigner\b0 :Signs APKs (Android application packages) with the appropriate cryptographic signatures.Ensures that APK signatures will be verified successfully on all platform versions supported by the APK.\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\par
Remember that these command-line tools are essential for efficient Android development, whether you\rquote re building apps, analyzing APKs, or managing virtual devices. \f1\par
