\ul\b OPTION 2: Download and install Android Studio\ulnone\par
\par
\fs24 Step 1 \b0 - Download Android Studio {{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://developer.android.com/studio }}{\fldrslt{https://developer.android.com/studio\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs24\par
\par
\b Step 2\b0  - Install on the system\par
\par
\b Step 3 \b0 - Start Android Studio\par
\par
\b Step 4 \b0 -More or  Go to "Tools" -> "SDK Manager" (or click on the SDK Manager icon in the toolbar)\par
\par
\b Step 5 \b0 - Select as per your testing needs\par
\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\b SDK Platforms: \b0 Select the desired Android API levels you want to target for your tests. You can choose multiple versions\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\b SDK Tools\b0 : Choose the platform-tools, build-tools, emulators etc compatible with your targeted API level(s) \par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\par
\b Step 6 \b0 - Click Apply and wait for setup to complete\par
\par
\b Step 7 \b0 - Set the folder having \b platform-tools, build-tools as ANDROID_HOME \b0 and update Path env variable\par
\par
\b Step 8 \b0 - Can run command appium-doctor --android to check all requirements for Android Testing are completed\par
\par

\pard\sl276\slmult1\ul\b Android Virtual Device (AVD) Setup for Automation\par
\par
\ulnone How to create and start AVD (emulator) with Android Studio GUI App\b0\par
\cf2\b\fs28\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl276\slmult1\cf0\fs24 Step 1 \b0 - Open Android Studio\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b Step 2 \b0 - Go to "Tools" -> "AVD Manager" (or click the AVD Manager icon in the toolbar)\par

\pard\sl276\slmult1          Or\par
        Android Studio > Preferences > Appearance & Behavior > System Settings > Android\par
                                           SDK > AVD Manager\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl276\slmult1\b Step 3 \b0 - Click "Create Virtual Device" and choose a desired device configuration (phone or tablet) with the required Android API level\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b Step 4 \b0 - Click "Next" and follow the steps to define the AVD configuration (name, RAM, storage etc.)\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b Step 5 \b0 - Click "Finish" to create the emulator\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b Step 6 \b0 - Launch the emulator from the AVD Manager\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}\b Step 7 \b0 - Check the emulator is available in Device Manager\par

\pard\sl276\slmult1      (Device manager will show all connected devices, virtual and physical)\cf2\b\fs28\par
